<Base title="About">
  <h1>About usnt.today</h1>
  <p>
    usnt.today shows which players eligible for the U.S. men's and women's national teams have games on
    a given day, and where to watch those games in the U.S.
  </p>

  <h2>Facts only</h2>
  <p>
    Schedules and results come from match data providers. Transfers and call-ups appear only after an
    official club, league or federation announcement, linked from each entry. No rumors.
  </p>

  <h2>Eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    Players are listed as Active (committed to the U.S.) or Eligible (not confirmed as committed to
    any country). Players in club squad data with U.S. nationality are added automatically as
    Eligible; editors add dual nationals listed under another country by hand. Each player's page
    names where the nationality information comes from. We report it; we don't verify it.
  </p>

  <h2>Coverage</h2>
  <p>
    Match data currently covers 12 competitions: the Premier League, Championship, Bundesliga, Serie A,
    La Liga, Ligue 1, Eredivisie, Primeira Liga, Brasileirão Série A, UEFA Champions League, European
    Championship and FIFA World Cup. MLS, NWSL and other leagues aren't covered yet. Results appear after
    the match; there are no live scores.
  </p>

  <h2>Not affiliated</h2>
  <p>usnt.today is independent and not affiliated with U.S. Soccer, its national teams, or any club or league.</p>

  <p><a href="/correction?page=%2Fabout">Suggest a correction</a></p>
</Base>
